===== 10 · reboot, then the scan a third time =====
  gold1 rebooted; then, on the first shell into it:
    $ limactl shell gold1 -- whoami
    This account is currently not available.        # the /sbin/nologin message
  the run's own record of why (step 8, the run as root):
    TASK [Ensure that System Accounts Do Not Run a Shell Upon Login - Disable Login Shell for System Accounts]
    changed: [gold1] => (item={'key': 'lab-user', 'value': ['x', '501', '1000', 'Lab User', '/home/lab-user.guest', '/bin/bash']})
  the login user's UID is 501 — inherited from the workstation; RHEL's UID_MIN is 1000, so the rule
  treats it as a system account and sets its shell to nologin. The only login account is now locked out.
  the scan cannot run a third time: there is no account to run it as. Last good scan is step 9 (fail 70).
  gold1 stopped; it is spent — a fresh boot from the image is needed for any further run.
